{
  "_comment": [
    "Copy this to sso.json beside the application's data and put your own client id in it.",
    "That copy is the only one the application reads - load_config is never handed the",
    "repository's directory - so a file here changes nothing at runtime.",
    "",
    "Register your own rather than reusing someone else's. The id is not a secret, but it",
    "is an identity. If every fork shipped one id, then as far as CCP are concerned every",
    "token on the planet belongs to that one application - one fork misbehaves and the rate",
    "limit is shared, a revocation kills everyone, and a ban lands on whoever registered it.",
    "",
    "Register a public native application with PKCE at https://developers.eveonline.com.",
    "There is no client secret, and there must not be: a secret in an open-source desktop",
    "application is a secret on every user's disk.",
    "",
    "The callback must be registered character-for-character as the redirect below. CCP",
    "match it exactly, which is also why the port is fixed - an ephemeral port cannot be",
    "registered in advance."
  ],
  "client_id": "",
  "callback_port": 47624,
  "redirect_uri_to_register": "http://localhost:47624/callback"
}
